                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f6460950-8250-4d4c-99c5-343b5ac5d3a6",
                        "source_entry_id": "af871e4d-fe8f-38e0-8a12-6ebd23119569",
                        "source_sense_id": "e0986184-ff2b-3cf1-b122-1c679fc1b81f",
                        "source_sense_description": "Abweichung von Gerechtigkeit und Rechtschaffenheit",
                        "target_lang_word": "iniquity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "iniquity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e636dd1-ebbd-38f4-b08f-22ddcdbede97",
                                        "entry_id": "ce7c4424-d685-360c-960e-e5efafa01e9f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Deviation from what is right; gross injustice, sin, wickedness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23ab0449-305d-4ad3-821a-25f18db239fa",
                                                "sense_id": "9e636dd1-ebbd-38f4-b08f-22ddcdbede97",
                                                "text": "And bycauſe our auncient enemye the Deuyl, who is the well and, ſpryng of iniquitie, and is not onely hymſelfe an homycide, a lyer, and and^([sic]) hater of the truth frõ the beginnyng: [...] Therefore like as we deſyre here to be delyuered from ſynne, ſo also we deſyre, that our heauenly father will ſaue vs, and defende vs from this euil the cauſer of ſynne, that is to ſaye, the Deuyll: [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "510a68dd-6fd9-4de7-b14b-441d4770e130",
                                                "sense_id": "9e636dd1-ebbd-38f4-b08f-22ddcdbede97",
                                                "text": "If you be ſo fond ouer her iniquity, giue her patent to offend, for if it touches not you, it comes neere no body."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54070b48-3341-4834-9f60-2791622c351c",
                                                "sense_id": "9e636dd1-ebbd-38f4-b08f-22ddcdbede97",
                                                "text": "Beholde, he putteth no truſt in his Saints, yea, the heauens are not cleane in his ſight. How much more abominable and filthie is man, which drinketh iniquitie like water?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb6cda7e-2b84-4d00-8e3a-a82101cce374",
                                                "sense_id": "9e636dd1-ebbd-38f4-b08f-22ddcdbede97",
                                                "text": "It will be found, when the Myſterie of iniquitie ſhall be unriddled, that, as they were their ſpawn the Anabaptiſts, the obſtructers of our Doctrinal Reformation, ſo, they are by their Miſſionaries ſent unto Corners and Hillie Countreys the obſtructers of our practical."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a18662a3-522f-488d-9020-e92f13f328aa",
                                                "sense_id": "9e636dd1-ebbd-38f4-b08f-22ddcdbede97",
                                                "text": "In the scanty number of reclaimed convicts, the noted George Barrington holds a conspicuous place. [...] His death took place nearly seven years ago: but for a considerable time previously he was in a state of insanity, produced, it is believed, by serious and sorrowful reflections on his early career of iniquity. [...] [H]is death was that of a sincere Christian."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11deb0c8-4d10-44c9-8ce0-0858629cb37d",
                                                "sense_id": "9e636dd1-ebbd-38f4-b08f-22ddcdbede97",
                                                "text": "It is one of the most surprising things that I have ever observed, That sanctity should be ashamed to look out, but iniquity show itself at noon. [...] Hence the company of rakes over their bottle, are not shy to open to another the mystery of iniquity in their most abandoned actions, and to glory in their shame."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32f41354-a8d4-4172-8154-a5465fe9ddea",
                                                "sense_id": "9e636dd1-ebbd-38f4-b08f-22ddcdbede97",
                                                "text": "Nekhlúdoff awoke next morning feeling as if he had been guilty of some iniquity the day before. He began considering. He could not remember having done anything wrong; he had committed no evil act, but he had had evil thoughts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbb0e66b-90e4-45cf-8bd2-a48e44cc665e",
                                                "sense_id": "9e636dd1-ebbd-38f4-b08f-22ddcdbede97",
                                                "text": "But ever since the concept of \"hamartia\" recurred through Aristotle's Poetics, in an attempt to describe man's ingrained iniquity, our impulse has been to identify a telling defect in those brought suddenly and dramatically low."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "586e40f4-9048-3645-8f82-61a14ab3b2d4",
                                        "entry_id": "ce7c4424-d685-360c-960e-e5efafa01e9f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act of great injustice or unfairness; a sinful or wicked act; an unconscionable deed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "906d8753-462b-488f-a7ed-1570461dddd9",
                                                "sense_id": "586e40f4-9048-3645-8f82-61a14ab3b2d4",
                                                "text": "For this is an heinous crime, yea, it is an iniquitie to bee puniſhed by the Judges."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0840213d-836e-4d69-8411-1a1c88013d19",
                                                "sense_id": "586e40f4-9048-3645-8f82-61a14ab3b2d4",
                                                "text": "[A]s for the other [goat], which was the Scape Goat, he [Aaron] was to lay his hands on the head thereof, and by a confeſſion of the iniquities of the people, to lay them all on that head, and then by ſome opportune man, to cauſe the Goat to be led into the wilderneſſe, and there to eſcape, and carry away with him the iniquities of the people."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d281d9a-2f2c-4cdf-a224-2d7744cae079",
                                                "sense_id": "586e40f4-9048-3645-8f82-61a14ab3b2d4",
                                                "text": "O regard not this, 'tis an iniquity to be taken heed of, in a dark day, in a day of trouble, ſuch as was upon Job; as black a day was upon him, as ever upon any in the world, as to his perſonal condition."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de4ecf15-a272-4ae8-a114-e7ce9ebd8bb6",
                                                "sense_id": "586e40f4-9048-3645-8f82-61a14ab3b2d4",
                                                "text": "As for moral Actions, a good Beginning is a great Sign of a good End; but it cannot juſtify a bad one, upon any Attempt: For there's many a holy Cheat in the World; and many an Iniquity, countenanc'd with Religion and Self-Preſervation, which is carry'd on under that Mask, to Rebellion and Murder."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a8299f0-d173-4499-a5c7-a34dbf3ec045",
                                                "sense_id": "586e40f4-9048-3645-8f82-61a14ab3b2d4",
                                                "text": "I would say that Slavery was an iniquity, and ought to be abolished. I would say there was no reason nor justice in the law, or the constitution that allows one man to hold another man in bondage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6db3c2db-343d-4774-b95e-4e707be6f2b5",
                                                "sense_id": "586e40f4-9048-3645-8f82-61a14ab3b2d4",
                                                "text": "The path of the righteous man is beset on all sides by the iniquities of the selfish and the tyranny of evil men."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fde60c13-cf4a-49b5-b7a8-616a62b99892",
                        "source_entry_id": "af871e4d-fe8f-38e0-8a12-6ebd23119569",
                        "source_sense_id": "e0986184-ff2b-3cf1-b122-1c679fc1b81f",
                        "source_sense_description": "Abweichung von Gerechtigkeit und Rechtschaffenheit",
                        "target_lang_word": "iniquité",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "iniquité",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "81e3631e-b487-3074-a7ef-482fa455b2ac",
                                        "entry_id": "90be4860-c803-37c5-bd37-8abe0a96c348",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Vice de ce qui est inique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d95f957b-b131-4460-a64a-17bc28729605",
                                                "sense_id": "81e3631e-b487-3074-a7ef-482fa455b2ac",
                                                "text": "Ô victime, tu sais le sinistre dessein\nD’Iahvèh m’aveuglant du feu de sa colère.\nL’iniquité divine est ton seul assassin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9aa4dd2f-85f7-411c-81af-527bb183dc25",
                                                "sense_id": "81e3631e-b487-3074-a7ef-482fa455b2ac",
                                                "text": "L’iniquité de certains jugements. — C’est le comble de l’iniquité."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36f58ef1-507a-380b-9da7-c7db35dbddc5",
                                        "entry_id": "90be4860-c803-37c5-bd37-8abe0a96c348",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Acte d’une injustice excessive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0776e451-4878-4471-9d00-d944754cb08d",
                                                "sense_id": "36f58ef1-507a-380b-9da7-c7db35dbddc5",
                                                "text": "Tant que l’homme est comprimé, tant que la contrainte des iniquités sociales le maintient prostré, l’on est en droit d’espérer beaucoup de l’inéclos qu’il porte en lui."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3584599-43ca-4a29-956c-9efc00134b28",
                                                "sense_id": "36f58ef1-507a-380b-9da7-c7db35dbddc5",
                                                "text": "Admettre cette préséance, c’est léser l’esprit républicain, porter atteinte aux principes de 89, faire fi des sacrifices consentis par les révolutionnaires de 1830 à 1871, c’est accepter de voir rétablir les iniquités qu’ils ont combattues au prix de leur sang !"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "854029a5-aa47-4b66-82d8-53b2f6ba75fa",
                                                "sense_id": "36f58ef1-507a-380b-9da7-c7db35dbddc5",
                                                "text": "L’iniquité la plus terrible, si elle est commise dans un aveugle emportement, l’homme qui mérite ce nom peut s’en souvenir le front haut quand il l’a reconnue devant Allah le Magnanime et surtout devant lui-même. Mais il sera interdit à jamais de se regarder dans son cœur et dans son âme à celui qui mène jusqu’au bout l’injustice qu’il a méditée, calculée, exécutée de sang-froid."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3601533-43c0-4d58-ad8b-05a371d58e0b",
                                                "sense_id": "36f58ef1-507a-380b-9da7-c7db35dbddc5",
                                                "text": "Et les intellectuels ? […] Mais pour eux, il n’est pas mille façons d’envisager les iniquités en chaîne que déclenche le grippage du capitalisme."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8202cab0-ef09-3d68-be70-c6e1a5f2ca12",
                                        "entry_id": "90be4860-c803-37c5-bd37-8abe0a96c348",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "État de péché, la corruption des mœurs, le débordement des vices."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f78b310b-f575-4a7d-a717-ce01a604379a",
                                                "sense_id": "8202cab0-ef09-3d68-be70-c6e1a5f2ca12",
                                                "text": "[…] et, tout en lui imposant une pénitence qui puisse le purifier de son iniquité, nous tournons le tranchant aigu de notre indignation sur le maudit instrument qui a failli entraîner sa perte absolue."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "55cce500-9aea-314c-b646-fd67c72a9842",
                                        "entry_id": "90be4860-c803-37c5-bd37-8abe0a96c348",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Péchés, actes contraires à la religion, à la morale."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aadc7dd6-5b7f-4135-acbe-dcfe1bd13855",
                                                "sense_id": "55cce500-9aea-314c-b646-fd67c72a9842",
                                                "text": "Les enfants portent souvent la peine des iniquités de leurs pères."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
